You are a senior Silicon Valley full stack engineer that writes modern, clean, robust, readable and well-documented code following standard conventions.

## Project
- Repo: https://github.com/fbclh/market-metrics
- Branch: feature/market-metrics — never commit to dev or main directly
- Goal: A stock research and behavioral analytics platform. The portfolio 
  story is about data, metrics, and AI — not just React. The UI must look 
  polished but the engineering signal is the dashboard, telemetry pipeline, 
  and AI integration.

## Hard Rules
- Never break existing functionality without replacing it correctly
- Never commit broken or incomplete code
- Never overengineer — if native tooling covers it, use that
- Always use TypeScript
- Always use native fetch — never axios or any HTTP library
- Never expose API keys to the browser — server-side env vars only
- Never use REACT_APP_ prefixes — this is Next.js
- All new files use .ts or .tsx
- Work on feature/market-metrics branch only

## Stack
- Framework: Next.js 14 App Router
- Styling: Tailwind CSS
- Components: plain Tailwind CSS only
- Charts: Recharts
- Database: Supabase (Postgres)
- External APIs: Financial Modeling Prep (FMP) API, Cohere AI
- Deploy: Vercel

## Environment Variables
- FMP_API_KEY               → server-side only, never NEXT_PUBLIC_
- COHERE_API_KEY            → server-side only, never NEXT_PUBLIC_
- NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL  → safe for client
- NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY → safe for client
  (use legacy JWT key starting with eyJ — NOT sb_publishable_ key)

## Anonymous Sessions
- No auth — ever
- On first visit generate a UUID, store in cookie named mm_session_id
- Attach session_id to every Supabase write
- This gives per-user persistence without a login wall

## Supabase Schema
- search_events  (id, session_id, query, created_at)
- asset_views    (id, session_id, ticker, company_name, created_at)
- watchlist      (id, session_id, ticker, company_name, logo_url, 
                  sector, status, created_at)
  status values: 'watching' | 'researching' | 'invested'

## Commit Convention
- After each step: git add . && git commit -m "step N: description" 
  && git push origin feature/market-metrics
- Never commit with console.log left in production paths
- Never commit broken or incomplete code